---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/withBase';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Space Nerd — purpose, limitations, and where to verify spaceflight facts."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-24 md:px-8">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Space Nerd"
      title="About this site"
      subtitle="Space Nerd is a static, editorial overview—designed to feel calm and readable, not exhaustive."
    />

    <figure class="mb-10 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-900/60">
      <img
        src={withBase('/images/vab-building.jpg')}
        alt="NASA Vehicle Assembly Building at Kennedy Space Center with the large American flag"
        class="h-64 w-full object-cover object-center md:h-96"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-500">
        Photo:
        <a
          href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VAB_and_SLS.jpg"
          class="ml-1 text-slate-400 underline-offset-2 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Wikimedia Commons (NASA)
        </a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-slate-300">
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        The shuttle pages summarize orbiter histories at a high level. The planet pages compress enormous fields of
        science into short intros. The Moon section highlights Apollo’s arc without replacing archives, oral histories,
        or peer-reviewed sources.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        For mission specifics, engineering details, and official timelines, start with{' '}
        <a
          href="https://www.nasa.gov"
          class="text-nebula underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          NASA
        </a>{' '}
        and museum partners. Wikipedia can be a useful map to primary sources—treat it as a signpost, not a citation.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        Imagery on this site includes the Apollo 17 “Blue Marble” photograph (public domain), served locally for
        performance. Credit lines appear near images and in the footer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Colophon</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
        Built with{' '}
        <a href="https://astro.build" class="text-nebula hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Astro</a
        >
        and{' '}
        <a href="https://tailwindcss.com" class="text-nebula hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Tailwind CSS</a
        >. Typography: Syne (display) and DM Sans (body), served via Google Fonts.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
